fuse2fs: do not include <linux/xattr.h> in addition to <sys/xattr.h>

With uClibc-ng, <linux/xattr.h> defines XATTR_CREATE/XATTR_REPLACE as
numeric macros, then the enum of <sys/xattr.h> no longer compiles
("expected identifier before numeric constant"). <sys/xattr.h> is enough.

--- a/misc/fuse2fs.c
+++ b/misc/fuse2fs.c
@@ -16,7 +16,6 @@
 #ifdef __linux__
 # include <linux/fs.h>
 # include <linux/falloc.h>
-# include <linux/xattr.h>
 #endif
 #ifdef HAVE_SYS_XATTR_H
 #include <sys/xattr.h>
